  "verbalization": "Osugacestat is implicated in the pathogenesis of SK-VLB through a multi-step mechanism involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1. This enzyme is a target of both Osugacestat and 3-Phenylpiperidine, which in turn targets SK-VLB. The presence of multiple pathways converging on UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1 suggests a potential role in the regulation of SK-VLB, possibly through the modification of substrates that influence its activity. The shared target of Osugacestat and Cespitulactam K further supports the notion of a common pathway, though the specific mechanism by which these compounds interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1 remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Osugacestat and SK-VLB, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the molecular interactions that underlie this connection.",
